Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:19:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 13/15] shader: VICTORY_WAVE64_REDUCE takes reductions in
 IR-uniform control flow

The 5 low-rate wave-reduction refusals (0a5d4f90, a53a7977, 1369868128,
ce2378e5, be14e72d; 4/4/2/2/0 dispatches a frame, the post-process cadence)
stop at 'a wave reduction over both 32-lane halves' because the reduction's
block is not in in_step: the loop counts are not proven alike, though every
branch on the path is on a scalar (uniform_control).

With VICTORY_WAVE64_REDUCE=1, when the reduction is not inside a nested
guard block (cur == level) and every path to its block goes through scalar
branches only, the halves reduce their own 32 lanes and exchange the result
through threadgroup memory with a group barrier (the existing
reduce_across), instead of refusing. Lane branches still refuse: they split
the wave, and a barrier there could hang. Off by default; part of the shader
cache key.

Host tests: uniform_control follows a scalar branch and rejects both sides
of a lane (v_cmpx + s_cbranch_execz) branch. Build checked to target-b with
DXC (indirect-clamp.dxil 5,244 B); target/ was not touched.
